=== Prompt ===
Who is Batman?

=== Response ===
Batman is a fictional superhero created by Bob Kane and Bill Finger. Originally appearing in comic books published by DC Comics, Batman has since appeared in various forms of media, including movies, television series, and video games.

Batman's alter ego is Bruce Wayne, a wealthy philanthropist and business magnate who resides in Gotham City. After witnessing the murder of his parents as a child, Bruce dedicates his life to fighting crime and injustice. He trains his body and mind to peak physical and intellectual levels, and uses his wealth to fund a secret identity as a crime-fighting vigilante.

Batman is known for his distinctive costume, which includes a cape, cowl, and utility belt, and for his use of martial arts, detective skills, and high-tech gadgets in his fight against crime. He is often depicted as a complex and brooding character, with a strong sense of justice and a desire to protect the innocent.

Batman is one of the most popular and enduring characters in comic book history, and has been a cultural icon for over 80 years. He has been portrayed by a number of actors in live-action films and television series, including Michael Keaton, Val Kilmer, George Clooney, Christian Bale, Ben Affleck, and Robert Pattinson.

